/* AlarmX string table.
   Every user-facing string lives here. Nothing is hardcoded in components, so
   adding Tamil/Telugu/Bengali/Marathi later is a data change, not a rebuild.

   Default locale is hi-Latn (Hinglish) — Roman-script Hindi. It needs no font
   or keyboard support and is how the target user actually reads and texts.
   Tone rule: write how people text, not translated English.

   bn and ta arrive with the regional calendar (PRD 16). They are here because
   showing a Vishuddha Siddhanta panjika inside English chrome is incoherent,
   not because of a guess about where installs land. Scripts render with the
   system Noto fonts — bundling font files would blow the APK budget.  */

